 "body": "We are experiencing a very strange with the performance on queries with low limits. If the limit goes above 1024 the query is very fast, below its very slow:\r\n\r\n- Neo4j version: 4.4.29\r\n- Operating system: Ubuntu 18/22\r\n- API/Driver: Neo4j Browser (but the same thing using any BOLT driver.)\r\n\r\nWe are running this on a core cluster members browser (not the leader), using BOLT, without any routing.\r\n\r\n```\r\nPROFILE MATCH (environment:Environment{Id: \"3s736b3-08b3-4c0c-ae2e-33304faf28\" })-[:CREATED_ASSET]->(asset:Asset)\r\nRETURN asset ORDER BY asset.ChangedOn DESC LIMIT 10\r\n```\r\n\r\n`Started streaming 10 records after 7 ms and completed after 1915 ms.`\r\n\r\n![plan (1)](https://github.com/neo4j/neo4j/assets/11192051/4b6b3bba-93ca-45b1-aa1e-8b93ecf7502e)\r\n\r\n\r\nIf we run the exact same query with a 10K limit, it's way faster:\r\n\r\n```\r\nPROFILE MATCH (environment:Environment{Id: \"3s736b3-08b3-4c0c-ae2e-33304faf28\" })-[:CREATED_ASSET]->(asset:Asset)\r\nRETURN asset ORDER BY asset.ChangedOn DESC 10000\r\n```\r\n\r\n`Started streaming 10000 records after 31 ms and completed after 45 ms.`\r\n\r\n![plan](https://github.com/neo4j/neo4j/assets/11192051/8953fddc-cbfa-4424-8c39-be17a6bc67d2)\r\n\r\nThe query plans follow the same route. In our testing we find out that the limit is around 1024. After that the query speeds drops to the fast levels.",
